cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this audit, please cite the manuscript listed below."
title: "Protocol Choices, Not Method Quality, Decide the Ranking: A Reproducibility Audit of Remote Sensing Super-Resolution Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  A zero-training audit of 170 existing runs across four standard remote sensing
  super-resolution benchmarks, combined with a report-practice survey of 35 papers
  from 2026. The audit measures how often a method ranking changes when only the
  metric, the aggregation rule, the training seed, or the baseline convention is
  varied, and reduces the findings to a seven-item reproducibility scorecard.
  Submitted to IEEE JSTARS as an IEEE Regular Paper.
authors:
